&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clackamas County, Ore. (Jan. 9, 2026)-&lt;/strong&gt; On Thursday, January 8, 2026, at 12:46 p.m., Oregon State Police responded to a single-vehicle crash on Interstate 205, near milepost 15, in Clackamas County.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
The preliminary investigation indicated a northbound Ford Aspire, operated by Jack Jay Lewis (64) of Molalla, left the roadway for unknown reasons, struck an ODOT sign, and rolled.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The operator for the Ford (Lewis), who was not wearing a seatbelt, was declared deceased at the scene.&lt;/p&gt;

